            <div xml:id="d497">

                <pb facs="0777" n="651" sameAs="frus:frus1925v01/pg651"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.5045/63: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Consul General at
                        Shanghai</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Cunningham</hi>)</head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1925-06-04T17:00:00-04:00"><hi rendition="#italic">June 4, 1925—5
                                p.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>Your June 4, 6 p.m. and previous telegrams same subject.</p>
                <p>Department approves the measures taken by you and the Commander-in-Chief as
                    reported by you for the protection of the lives and property of American
                    citizens at Shanghai. Conferences have taken place here with a view to affording
                    further facilities for this purpose should they be necessary. While regretting
                    the turn of events, the Department is anxious that all needful measures should
                    be employed to prevent the further spread of the trouble and to afford adequate
                    protection to American lives and property. Should any action be contemplated
                    which goes beyond this function Department desires to be promptly informed.</p>
                <pb facs="0778" n="652" xml:id="pg652"/>
                <p>Department suggests that in telegraphing the Legation concerning developments at
                    Shanghai you state whether similar information is being telegraphed the
                    Department. This will avoid duplication. Repeat to Peking.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Kellogg</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
